        instruction: { zh: "有时对手落子后，你会想知道它是否有害以及是否需要应对。如果没有害处，你完全可以下在其他地方。这种下在别处的做法称为脱先。因此脱先时，你不对对手的棋进行防守回应，而是下在其他地方。这里白棋1大幅跳入黑棋领地。白棋威胁着在A点连接此子与其他白棋。如果黑棋想阻止这一连接，应该应对白1并在A点落子。白1之后在A点落子是否是好的回应，还是脱先更好？", en: "Sometimes your opponent plays a move, that makes you wonder if it does any harm and if you should react to it. If it does not do any harm, you can play a good move completely somewhere else. This playing somewhere else we call tenuki. So with tenuki you do not respond to the move of your opponent with a defensive move, but you play somewhere else. Here, White jumps with move 1 far into the black territory. White threatens to connect this stone with the other white stones by playing at A. If Black wants to prevent this, he should react to white 1 by playing at A. Is playing at A a good reply to white 1 or is it better to play tenuki?" },
